Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:05:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AI: cooperative deadline for the ability evaluation

chooseSpellAbilityToPlayFromList bounds its own cost by running the
evaluation on a thread and waiting with a timed future.get(). That only
works where threads are real. Under GraalVM Web Image the evaluation runs
on the caller (patch 0001), get() finds the future already done and the
timeout never fires, so one decision would have no ceiling.

Bound it cooperatively as well, in the loop that already checks for an
interrupt, against a deadline of the same getAITimeout(). The check runs
between candidate abilities: a single pathologically slow evaluation can
still overrun it. On a threaded runtime the existing cancel/stop still
covers that case.

Original-author: khaliostr (GitHub)
Origin: witchesofthehill/forge@026be2f808cffa77a39e52fb60e90869396164ed
(GPL-3.0-or-later). Adapted to Card-Forge/forge@ed0333f (where the loop no
longer has the timeoutReached flag) for OpenMana on 2026-09-24.
---
 forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/AiController.java | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/AiController.java b/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/AiController.java
index eab9fb89..78522000 100644
--- a/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/AiController.java
+++ b/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/AiController.java
@@ -1596,11 +1596,19 @@ public class AiController {
             Sentry.captureMessage(ex.getMessage() + "\nAssertionError [verifyTransitivity]: " + assertex);
         }
 
+        // OpenMana patch 0002 (2026-09-24, adapted from witchesofthehill/forge@026be2f):
+        // the time limit below is a thread plus a timed future.get(). Without
+        // real threads (GraalVM Web Image) the evaluation runs on the caller and
+        // that limit never fires, so a single decision would have no ceiling.
+        // Bound it cooperatively as well: one clock read per candidate ability.
+        final long evalDeadline = System.currentTimeMillis() + game.getAITimeout() * 1000L;
+
         FutureTask<SpellAbility> future = new FutureTask<>(() -> {
             //avoid ComputerUtil.aiLifeInDanger in loops as it slows down a lot.. call this outside loops will generally be fast...
             boolean isLifeInDanger = useLivingEnd && ComputerUtil.aiLifeInDanger(player, true, 0);
             for (final SpellAbility sa : ComputerUtilAbility.getOriginalAndAltCostAbilities(all, player)) {
-                if (Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()) {
+                if (Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()
+                        || System.currentTimeMillis() > evalDeadline) {
                     break;
                 }
 
